/-!
# Tensor closure of rational localizing categories

Source: literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/
`sk-thm-sf-pf-field/sk-thm-sf-pf-field-tensor.md` (blueprint: det-thm-sf-pf-field-tensor).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped CategoryTheory.Obj
open AlgebraicGeometry Scheme

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CondensedRing

/-- The bounded constructible rational coefficient category is closed under derived tensor,
and its localizing closure is closed under derived tensor.

Source: literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/
`sk-thm-sf-pf-field/sk-thm-sf-pf-field-tensor.md` (blueprint: det-thm-sf-pf-field-tensor).

The coefficient hypothesis `hΛ` identifies `Λ` with the condensed ring of `E` or of the
finite-subextension-valued `Q̄_ℓ` as commutative monoid objects (an isomorphism in `Mon`), so
the ring structure of `Λ`, not only its underlying abelian sheaf, is the node's.

Proof plan, following the node:
1. The K-flat derived tensor of `sk-def-sfb-derived-tensor-hom` is exact in each variable
   (a K-flat representative sends cone triangles to cone triangles and shifts to shifts) and
   preserves the ambient small coproducts of `det-def-localizing-closure-existence` (1), by its
   internal-Hom right adjoint; the Koszul symmetry gives the same in the other variable.
2. `X` is Noetherian (finite type over `Spec k`), so `det-cor-coefficient-heart-ii-generation`
   applies: `Dbc` is triangulated and generated by finite cones of shifts of `a_! L` with `a`
   locally closed and `L` lisse in degree zero. Two finite-cone inductions reduce clause (1)
   to `a_! L ⊗ᴸ b_! M`.
3. Open-closed base change (`det-sf-open-closed-sequence-ring-sheaf` (4)) and the
   factorization independence of `lem-sfb-locally-closed-extension-coherence` give
   `a^* b_! M ≃ c_! d^* M` for `W = S ×_X T`, `c : W → S`, `d : W → T`.
4. Two applications of the projection formula `det-lem-int-tensor-projection` give
   `a_! L ⊗ᴸ b_! M ≃ a_! c_! (c^* L ⊗ᴸ d^* M)`.
5. Lisse sheaves are locally finite free, hence flat and K-flat in degree zero, so
   `c^* L ⊗ᴸ d^* M` is the underived tensor, a lisse sheaf `N`.
6. `a_! c_! N` restricts to `0, 0, 0, 0, N` on the five locally closed pieces
   `X \ Z, Z \ S, S \ V, V \ W, W`; this finite stratification makes it constructible
   (`sk-lem-coefficient-heart`), hence in `Dbc`. With step 2 this proves clause (1).
7. For `B ∈ Dbc`, the objects `A` with `A ⊗ᴸ B ∈ Loc(Dbc)` form a localizing subcategory
   (step 1) containing `Dbc` (clause (1)); minimality in
   `det-def-localizing-closure-existence` (2) gives it for all `A ∈ Loc(Dbc)`.
8. For fixed `A ∈ Loc(Dbc)`, the objects `B` with `A ⊗ᴸ B ∈ Loc(Dbc)` form a localizing
   subcategory containing `Dbc` by step 7; minimality again gives clause (2).
-/
theorem tensorClosureRational
    (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime]
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (p : ℕ) [CharP k p]
    (hp : 0 < p) (hpl : p ≠ ℓ)
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (aX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsSeparated aX] [LocallyOfFiniteType aX] [QuasiCompact aX]
    (Λ : Sheaf (coherentTopology Profinite.{u}) Ab.{u + 1})
    [MonObj Λ] [IsCommMonObj Λ]
    (hΛ : (∃ E : PadicAlgCl.FiniteIntermediateField ℓ,
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousMapRingObj E))) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.padicAlgClRingObj ℓ))) :
    (∀ (K M : DerivedCategory
        (Mod (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology X) Ab.{u + 1})
          (condensedRingObj Λ X))),
      constantModelBoundedConstructible Λ X K →
      constantModelBoundedConstructible Λ X M →
      constantModelBoundedConstructible Λ X
        (((derivedTensor Λ X).obj K).obj M)) ∧
    (∀ (A B : DerivedCategory
        (Mod (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology X) Ab.{u + 1})
          (condensedRingObj Λ X))),
      CategoryTheory.localizingClosure
          (constantModelBoundedConstructible Λ X) A →
      CategoryTheory.localizingClosure
          (constantModelBoundedConstructible Λ X) B →
      CategoryTheory.localizingClosure
          (constantModelBoundedConstructible Λ X)
            (((derivedTensor Λ X).obj A).obj B)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CondensedRing
